Breast Cancer
Lump or thickening in the breast or underarm, change in breast size/shape, dimpling of skin, nipple discharge (other than milk), nipple retraction, redness or scaling of the breast skin.

Lung Cancer
Persistent cough, coughing up blood, chest pain that worsens with deep breathing/coughing, hoarseness, unexplained weight loss, shortness of breath, wheezing, recurrent bronchitis/pneumonia.

Colorectal Cancer
Blood in stool (bright red or dark), persistent change in bowel habits (diarrhea/constipation), narrow stools, abdominal pain/cramps/bloating, unexplained weight loss, fatigue, feeling that bowel doesn’t empty completely.

Brain Cancer
New or changing headaches (often worse in morning), seizures, nausea/vomiting without other cause, vision/speech/hearing problems, balance or walking difficulty, weakness/numbness in one part of body, personality/memory changes.

Prostate Cancer
Frequent urination (especially at night), difficulty starting or stopping urine stream, weak/interrupted urine flow, painful/burning urination, blood in urine or semen, erectile dysfunction, pain in lower back/hips/thighs.

Eye Cancer (e.g., melanoma, retinoblastoma)
Blurred vision or sudden vision loss, flashes of light or floaters, dark spot on iris that grows, change in pupil shape, bulging of the eye, eye pain (late stage).

Liver Cancer
Unexplained weight loss, loss of appetite, upper abdominal pain (right side), feeling of fullness after small meal, nausea/vomiting, jaundice (yellow skin/eyes), white/gray stools, fatigue, abdominal swelling (ascites).

Cervical Cancer
Abnormal vaginal bleeding (after intercourse, between periods, after menopause), heavier/longer menstrual bleeding, watery/bloody vaginal discharge with foul odor, pelvic pain, pain during intercourse.

Skin Cancer
Melanoma: Asymmetrical mole, irregular border, varied color, diameter >6mm, evolving/changing.
Basal cell: Pearly/waxy bump, bleeding sore that heals and returns.
Squamous cell: Firm red nodule, scaly/crusted flat lesion. Any new pigmented spot or non-healing ulcer.

Pancreatic Cancer
Jaundice (dark urine, pale stools, itchy skin, yellow skin/eyes), upper abdominal or mid-back pain, unexplained weight loss, loss of appetite, new-onset diabetes, nausea/vomiting, blood clots, fatigue.